<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Moody's upgrades Australian Keystart bonds.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Moody's upgrades Australian Keystart bonds.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-12-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Moody's Investors Service said it upgraded the A$728 million of bonds issued by Keystart Bonds Ltd to Aaa from Aa1.  </p>
<p>Moody's said the upgrade of the mortgage backed securities was due to the upgrade of the State of Western Australia long term domestic currency rating on Monday, also to Aaa from AA1.</p>
<p>Keystart Bonds obligations are ultimately indemnified by the State of Western Australia, it added.</p>
<p>--Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
